  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "NATIVE-RUNTIME-01",
      "result": "Fresh r3 status and Claude bridge variants required",
      "detail": "The status helper and Claude bridge both hardcode the 20261006 installation and pass ResourceLimits to launch_worker. They retain the old f005 resource_limits module, whereas installed r3 contains reviewed de7 Job-limit ordering repair. Unchanged windows.py hash alone does not attest that dependency."
    },
    {
      "id": "NATIVE-RUNTIME-02",
      "result": "Exact r3 uv binding required",
      "detail": "Old wrappers/status support pin d6ebb pyvenv.cfg and validate the old stdlib format. r3 pins 0c2b pyvenv.cfg with six uv keys. Merely replacing the installation path is insufficient."
    },
    {
      "id": "NATIVE-RUNTIME-03",
      "result": "Generic Codex login must select r3 explicitly",
      "detail": "The protected generic helper exists with matching e3d hash and accepts InstallRoot. Its windows.login_worker path does not pass ResourceLimits, so this audit does not attribute the affinity-order failure to that path. Current guide nevertheless selects the old runtime. Its historical task/log lifecycle is unchanged by this audit."
    },
    {
      "id": "NATIVE-RUNTIME-04",
      "result": "Keep reviewed native provider contracts unchanged",
      "detail": "Codex status login status, Claude status --setting-sources empty auth status --json, Claude login --setting-sources empty auth login --claudeai, and Codex login --device-auth remain the reviewed argv. Agy isolated integration hold remains unchanged. This audit establishes no authentication state or serving-model readiness."
    }
